@lang en
-- Tests of ie-powers-duties-continuing.l4: s 10, s 22(1), s 22(2), s 23(1), s 23(2) and s 24.
-- Expected values were decided from the text of each section (quoted in the comments) and never from the code.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-powers-duties-continuing`

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      requires IS A BOOLEAN
      earlier IS A NUMBER
      ceased IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on`
`occasion` d requires earlier ceased MEANS
    `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on` WITH
        `the day of the occasion` IS d
        `the occasion requires it` IS requires
        `the number of earlier occasions on which it has already been used` IS earlier
        `the enactment has ceased to have effect before that day` IS ceased

GIVEN person IS A STRING
      first IS A DATE
      last IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `A holder of an office`
`holder` person first last MEANS
    `A holder of an office` WITH person IS person, `first day` IS first, `last day` IS last

-- Alice holds the office from 1 January 2026 to 30 June 2026 inclusive; Bob from 1 July 2026 on, with no end.
`Alice then Bob` MEANS LIST (`holder` "Alice" (YMD 2026 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30))), (`holder` "Bob" (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING)
-- Alice to 30 June, Bob from 5 July: nobody holds the office from 1 to 4 July.
`Alice, a vacancy, then Bob` MEANS LIST (`holder` "Alice" (YMD 2026 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30))), (`holder` "Bob" (YMD 2026 7 5) NOTHING)
-- Alice to 15 July, Bob from 1 July: both hold the office from 1 to 15 July.
`Alice and Bob overlapping` MEANS LIST (`holder` "Alice" (YMD 2026 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 7 15))), (`holder` "Bob" (YMD 2026 7 1) NOTHING)

§ `Section 10: "An enactment continues to have effect and may be applied from time to time as occasion requires"`

#ASSERT     `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 0 FALSE)
-- from time to time: an earlier use does not exhaust it, however many there have been
#ASSERT     `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 1 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 100 FALSE)
-- and no day is excluded
#ASSERT     `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 1900 1 1) TRUE 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2099 12 31) TRUE 0 FALSE)
-- "as occasion requires": where the occasion does not require it, the section gives nothing
#ASSERT NOT `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE 0 FALSE)
-- "continues to have effect": an enactment that has ceased to have effect is not applied on the strength of this section
#ASSERT NOT `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 0 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE 0 TRUE)

§ `Section 22(1): "A power conferred by an enactment may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires"`

#ASSERT     `a power conferred by an enactment may be exercised on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `a power conferred by an enactment may be exercised on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 11) TRUE 1 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `a power conferred by an enactment may be exercised on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 12) TRUE 100 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a power conferred by an enactment may be exercised on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a power conferred by an enactment may be exercised on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 0 TRUE)

§ `Section 23(1): "A duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires"`

#ASSERT     `a duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `a duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 11) TRUE 1 FALSE)
#ASSERT     `a duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 12) TRUE 100 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `a duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed on the occasion` (`occasion` (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE 0 TRUE)

§ `Section 22(2): a power conferred on the holder of an office as that holder is conferred on the holder for the time being`

-- who is the holder on a day
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS JUST "Alice"
-- Alice's last day is 30 June and Bob's first is 1 July: both ends are inclusive
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS JUST "Alice"
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 7 1)  `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS JUST "Bob"
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 1 1)  `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS JUST "Alice"
-- before anyone held it
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Bob has no last day
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2099 1 1) `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS JUST "Bob"
-- a vacancy: nobody is the holder, and the section does not say what follows
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `, the holders being` `Alice, a vacancy, then Bob` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 7 3) `, the holders being` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- F44: two holders on one day: the section speaks of "the holder", so the case is not answered
#ASSERT REFUSED `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 7 10) `, the holders being` `Alice and Bob overlapping` BECAUSE "section 22(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who exercises the power when two persons hold the office on the same day"
-- before the overlap, and after it, there is one holder
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, the holders being` `Alice and Bob overlapping` EQUALS JUST "Alice"
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office on` (YMD 2026 7 16) `, the holders being` `Alice and Bob overlapping` EQUALS JUST "Bob"

-- who may exercise the power: the person is the holder for the time being, and the power is conferred on the office
#ASSERT     `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Bob"   `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT     `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2026 7 1)  `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Bob"   `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2026 7 1)  `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
-- a power conferred on a named person and not on the holder as that holder: the section does not reach it
#ASSERT NOT `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` FALSE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
-- nobody holds the office: nobody has the power on this section
#ASSERT NOT `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Bob" `, the holders being` `Alice, a vacancy, then Bob`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the person may exercise the power on` (YMD 2026 7 10) `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice and Bob overlapping` BECAUSE "section 22(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who exercises the power when two persons hold the office on the same day"

§ `Section 23(2): a duty imposed on the holder of an office as that holder is imposed on the holder for the time being`

#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office, for a duty, on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS JUST "Alice"
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office, for a duty, on` (YMD 2026 7 1)  `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS JUST "Bob"
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office, for a duty, on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the holder for the time being of the office, for a duty, on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `, the holders being` `Alice, a vacancy, then Bob` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `the holder for the time being of the office, for a duty, on` (YMD 2026 7 10) `, the holders being` `Alice and Bob overlapping` BECAUSE "section 23(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who performs the duty when two persons hold the office on the same day"

#ASSERT     `the person shall perform the duty on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT NOT `the person shall perform the duty on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Bob"   `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT     `the person shall perform the duty on` (YMD 2026 7 1)  `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Bob"   `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT NOT `the person shall perform the duty on` (YMD 2026 7 1)  `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT NOT `the person shall perform the duty on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` FALSE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice then Bob`
#ASSERT NOT `the person shall perform the duty on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Alice" `, the holders being` `Alice, a vacancy, then Bob`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the person shall perform the duty on` (YMD 2026 7 10) `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` TRUE `, the person being` "Bob" `, the holders being` `Alice and Bob overlapping` BECAUSE "section 23(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who performs the duty when two persons hold the office on the same day"

§ `Section 24: rules of court for a jurisdiction an enactment confers, extends or varies`

-- arguments: what the enactment does to the jurisdiction; whether the authority has power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court; the day
#ASSERT     `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it confers a new jurisdiction on the court`       TRUE `, on the day` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT     `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it extends an existing jurisdiction of the court` TRUE `, on the day` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT     `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it varies an existing jurisdiction of the court`  TRUE `, on the day` (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- "at any time": the day makes no difference
#ASSERT     `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it confers a new jurisdiction on the court`       TRUE `, on the day` (YMD 1900 1 1)
#ASSERT     `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it confers a new jurisdiction on the court`       TRUE `, on the day` (YMD 2099 12 31)
-- the authority has no power to make rules for that court: the section does not give it one
#ASSERT NOT `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it confers a new jurisdiction on the court`       FALSE `, on the day` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it extends an existing jurisdiction of the court` FALSE `, on the day` (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- an enactment that does none of the three: the section is not engaged
#ASSERT NOT `the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` `it does none of those things` TRUE `, on the day` (YMD 2026 3 10)
